WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.795
Telo Ride 1 is one application, for one class. A second application was still built

00:00:07.795 --> 00:00:09.854
beside it: a marketing site.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.522
That site is removed. It sold races and experience points, which Telo Ride 1 does

00:00:15.522 --> 00:00:20.763
not have. Its seven components, its scripts and its build steps left with it.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.145
The workspace is now the ride app on five libraries. The world library stays,

00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:30.552
because riding in Ibiza needs it.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.997
The app itself did not change. Connect the bike, the class, the ride, and the result

00:00:40.997 --> 00:00:43.961
look and work as they did, in the same bundle.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.791
The class, on every screen from a phone to a desktop, exactly as before.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.662
Verify ran ten steps before, and nine now. One production build, and every spec,

00:01:04.662 --> 00:01:07.612
unit test and backend test still passes.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.920
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.116
nothing else.

00:01:19.461 --> 00:01:24.413
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:29.425
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:32.926
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:37.247
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
